  '<p class="gd-p">Visitors who are not signed in get one quick game: spin the wheel, scratch to reveal, quick blackjack, cup shuffle, Plinko, the card pack, coin flip, dice roll, slot machine, prize drop or mystery box. Every play wins a promo code or another go. To see the code they give a first name and an email (a mobile number is optional), so you get a lead. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.</p><section class="gd-task" id="discount-games-and-leads-what-the-visitor-sees" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What the visitor sees</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>On the 2nd page view (any page) or after 30 seconds on the site, whichever first, or (on a computer) when the mouse heads for the tabs. A card slides in at the bottom; on a phone it is a sheet at the bottom, never a full-screen block, and it always closes.</li><li>Never for someone signed in, never on booking, pay, sign or sign-in pages, never on the first page of a visit from a search engine on a phone, never over the cookie banner; no new game for someone already known by email or with a booking request in progress. Closed, another game comes back on the 3rd page view after the close or 2 minutes later, at most 4 in a visit, and again on their next visit.</li><li>After claiming a code: no game for the rest of that visit. A day after their latest claim the game comes back on their next visit with the usual timings, a new game and a new draw, and they can win another code. The day counts for the browser, the email, the mobile number and (in the request-to-book form) the account; within it the game says when they can play again. A visitor known only through their own claim still gets it; one known through a booking request, the chat, a sign-in or as a renter does not.</li><li>Won and not claimed: a small badge &quot;Your 5% off is saved&quot; with <b class="gd-ui">Get my code</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Play again</b> stays on the pages. On a later visit, at the moment a first game would show, the prize pops up by itself once as a small slide-in at the bottom (&quot;Your 5% off is still waiting&quot;, the same two buttons), never as a card over the page; closed, it does not come back in that visit. Until they claim it or the prize ends after 14 days.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Play again</b> on a prize not claimed: a new, different game with a new draw. They keep the better of the two prizes and the other is closed, so there is only ever one code to claim: the card says &quot;You won 15% off&quot; or &quot;You keep your 5% off&quot;. Once a visit and once a day (a setting).</li><li>Every play wins: 5% off (54 in 100), 10% off (25), another go (15), 15% off (4), $50 off a rental of 3 days or more (1), 25% off up to $150 (0.6), $100 off a rental of 4 days or more (0.3) or one free day on a rental of 3 days or more (0.1). The prize is decided before the game starts; the game only shows it. The short terms with the game list the prizes and say the chances differ.</li><li>Another go: the card says &quot;You won another go!&quot; and <b class="gd-ui">Play again</b> starts a second, different game whose prize is drawn from the discounts only, so it always ends in a code. One replay at a time; it is never a code itself. Closed before pressing it, the card offers it again next time.</li><li>The code (for example WIN-7KQ4-XM2P) comes off the rental charge only, up to $75 for a percentage, on one booking, within 7 days, one code a day per person, email, phone and device, never with another code. An earlier code not used yet stays good until it ends. The email with the code goes either way; a reminder goes 3 days before its last day and another the day before (Promo codes). Offers only with the marketing box ticked.</li><li>On this device the code fills itself into the promo code box of the request form. Like every promo code, the discount is shared with the owner in the split.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="discount-games-and-leads-leads" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Leads</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renter leads</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles: plays, claims, codes on booking requests, bookings, revenue and discounts from game codes in the last 30 days, then the same by game and by prize (Play again shows its plays; it has no claims).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each claim: when, the name (and &quot;on the site now&quot;), email and phone, the prize and game, the code and whether it is used (with the booking), marketing consent, and the visit: cars and pages viewed, minutes, city and device. A person who won again shows &quot;2nd code of 2&quot; under the name on each of their lines.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Contacted</b> (it is yours). <b class="gd-ui">Close</b> with a reason when there is nothing more to do. A booking with the code marks the lead converted by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A visitor who viewed 3 cars or more also gets a Sales task, for example &quot;Claimed 10% off, viewed 6 cars: Maya&quot;. It closes when the code goes on a request. A new code while that task is open is added to it, not a second task.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="discount-games-and-leads-contact-details-typed-into-forms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Contact details typed into forms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renter leads</b>, the card &quot;Typed into forms&quot; at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When someone types a name, email or phone into the request to book, the contact form, List your car, the owner application, Create an account, the discount game or the chat, it is saved as soon as each field is valid, even if they never press Send.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line: when, the name (and &quot;On the site now&quot;), email and phone, the form, and Sent or Not sent. &quot;Email not confirmed&quot; means the account was opened from the form and the person has not opened the link we emailed them yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">After 30 minutes without sending, Sales&#39; queue gets &quot;Unfinished request from Maya Chen: follow up&quot; (not raised from 23:00 to 07:00, the quiet hours of the site alerts); To do shows it on the Sales line of Your teams. Call or email them; the task closes by itself when they send the form, or after 7 days (Program settings, Forms: close a Sales follow-up nobody answered after). The person stays on this list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Only what they typed is saved, and never used for offers without their consent.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A new email gets an account at once (no password, email not confirmed) and one email &quot;Continue your request&quot; 30 minutes later, between 9:00 and 21:00. Until they open its link they cannot accept an offer, sign, pay or upload documents. An account never confirmed closes after 30 days; the lead stays. It is on by default; the times and the To do are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, the card &quot;Forms left unfinished&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="discount-games-and-leads-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Discount games</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>On or off, the cap for percentage codes ($75), how long a code is good for (7 days), when it shows (2nd page view, 30 seconds, exit intent), the days a visitor keeps their prize (14: closing never draws a new one, and a prize not claimed pops up again until then), the days after a claim before the game comes back (1; 0 is one code per person ever), how often Play again works on a prize not claimed (once a day; 0 turns it off), and the cars viewed for a Sales task (3). The reminders before a code ends are under Promo codes.</li><li>After a visitor closes a game, the next card shows on their 3rd page view after the close (any page) or 2 minutes later, whichever first; at most 4 in one visit, no daily cap unless you set one. A prize waiting for them pops up once a visit only. All are settings. Never on booking, payment or signing pages; the request-to-book form has its own game.</li><li>Prizes and games: each prize with its percent, dollars or free days, a minimum rental length, its cap and its chance, or Play again (another go, at most one); each game&#39;s weight (0 turns it off). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save prizes and games</b>. Codes already sent keep their value.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'usage-and-paid-usage', 'chapter', 'assistant', 'The plans CarmaCars runs on include a free allowance: AI, the website, image transformations, emails, the database and storage. When an allowance runs out, AI and photo features pause with a short message until it resets. Workers AI never runs into paid usage; for photos you are asked before anything is paid.

## The alerts

At 80% of an allowance you get one quiet card on **To do** and one email to the alert address. When it is used up, a second card and email.

1. Workers AI used up shows "Stopped for today, never paid": it starts again at midnight, Toronto time. There is nothing to allow.
2. A used-up image allowance shows "Included ... used up for this month: Allow paid usage". Press **Allow paid usage** to see what continuing costs at the current rates.
3. Choose until the end of today or this month, type the most it may cost (for example $1), and press the Allow button. Or press Keep paused.
4. Nobody answering keeps it paused: nothing is charged. Live chat goes to a person, AI copy waits with the template text, Turo emails are read by the rules, photos keep their original background, the assistant rests.
5. The website and the portals are never paused (that would stop bookings): their card shows the estimated cost, usually cents.

## Settings > Usage

Open **Settings**, then **Usage**: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.

1. Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app''s own record shows as Unmetered.
2. The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.
3. Press **Change the shares** to change the assistant''s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.
4. Press **Change the allowance** after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).
5. Database size and file storage are our own server''s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.
6. Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.

## Alerts by text and the banner

7. When a figure reaches 80% of its allowance, and again at 100% (the website''s CPU time also at 70%), every Admin with a verified phone gets a text, once per figure and level a month, outside the quiet hours. Turn it off in Program settings (Usage alerts: also text every Admin).
8. While a figure is at its warning level or past it, a banner at the top of **Today** says so: red past the allowance, amber before.

## Emails through Cloudflare first

9. The site''s emails go through Cloudflare Email Service first (3,000 a month included with Workers Paid), then Resend. Sign-in emails stay on Resend. Emails wait until midnight only when both are used. "Emails this month (Cloudflare)" counts them. It needs the one-time setup in docs/changes/2026-11-03-cloudflare-email.md.
10. "Texts this month (Quo)" counts the texts sent through the Quo API, about US$0.01 each, with the cost so far. The texts and the banner warn at 80% and 100% of the 300 a month set as the budget (**Change the allowance**).
', 'Usage and paid usage', 'Included allowances, the 80% and used-up alerts, Workers AI by feature (never paid), allowing paid usage for photos, what pauses and what never does.',
  'The plans CarmaCars runs on include a free allowance: AI, the website, image transformations, emails, the database and storage. When an allowance runs out, AI and photo features pause with a short message until it resets. Workers AI never runs into paid usage; for photos you are asked before anything is paid.

## The alerts

At 80% of an allowance you get one quiet card on **To do**. When it is used up, a second card. Usage alerts are never emailed (they used to count against the emails they warned about); the banner, the cards and the Usage page show them.

1. Workers AI used up shows "Stopped for today, never paid": it starts again at midnight, Toronto time. There is nothing to allow.
2. A used-up image allowance shows "Included ... used up for this month: Allow paid usage". Press **Allow paid usage** to see what continuing costs at the current rates.
3. Choose until the end of today or this month, type the most it may cost (for example $1), and press the Allow button. Or press Keep paused.
4. Nobody answering keeps it paused: nothing is charged. Live chat goes to a person, AI copy waits with the template text, Turo emails are read by the rules, photos keep their original background, the assistant rests.
5. The website and the portals are never paused (that would stop bookings): their card shows the estimated cost, usually cents.

## Settings > Usage

Open **Settings**, then **Usage**: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.

1. Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app''s own record shows as Unmetered.
2. The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.
3. Press **Change the shares** to change the assistant''s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.
4. Press **Change the allowance** after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).
5. Database size and file storage are our own server''s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.
6. Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.

## Alerts by text and the banner

7. When a figure reaches 80% of its allowance, and again at 100% (the website''s CPU time also at 70%), every Admin with a verified phone gets a text, once per figure and level a month, outside the quiet hours. Turn it off in Program settings (Usage alerts: also text every Admin).
8. The banner at the top of **Today** speaks in money. The website, requests, storage and texts are billed by use and never paused: their banner is red only when this month''s projected cost above the allowance reaches US$5 (Program settings, Usage: red banner and alert only from), and then you also get the text. Under it, one quiet grey line with the cost (usually cents) and no text. Workers AI, photos and Claude (they stop or pause) and the emails (held at 100 a day) keep their banner: red when used up, amber before.

## Emails through Cloudflare first

9. The site''s emails go through Cloudflare Email Service first (3,000 a month included with Workers Paid), then Resend. Sign-in emails stay on Resend. Emails wait until midnight only when both are used. "Emails this month (Cloudflare)" counts them. It needs a one-time setup: the **Emails** card at the top of the Usage page (open **Settings**, then **Usage**) says whether Cloudflare sends and, when it does not, lists the four steps; the emails banner links to them, and every deploy lists the step until it is done.
10. "Texts this month (Quo)" counts the texts sent through the Quo API, about US$0.01 each, with the cost so far. The texts and the banner warn at 80% and 100% of the 300 a month set as the budget (**Change the allowance**).
